/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 84 0 R
/E (However, the challenge extends beyond the conflict itself. Even when fighting stops, recovering food systems takes years. Displaced farming communities struggle to return, landmines contaminate agricultural land, and economic collapse makes rebuilding nearly impossible without sustained international support.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
172 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 84 0 R
/E (Food insecurity in conflict areas is one of the most urgent humanitarian crises in the world. Wars and armed conflicts destroy farms, block food deliveries, collapse economies, displace families, and prevent humanitarian aid from reaching people in need. In an MUN, delegates must discuss how the international community can protect civilians, ensure access to food, and prevent famine.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
